# Trivy ignore file — acknowledged CVEs for the Trivy scans.
#
# Add a CVE ID on its own line, each with a justification comment above it.
# Entries here suppress findings in the filesystem and image scans of
# security.yml and in the "Snapshot build" scan.
# Keep this list short and review it regularly.
#
# Example:
#   # CVE-0000-00000 — false positive: package not reachable at runtime.
#   CVE-0000-00000

# CVE-2026-112366 (GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf), picomatch: in what ships, reached only through @parcel/watcher of
# next-intl's message extractor, which the web does not turn on; elsewhere through development tools that match
# the repository's own patterns. No patched release exists. Justification and expiry: .github/scripts/audit-allowlist.json.
CVE-2026-112366
